      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "The frame-header parser first materializes the attacker-controlled per-plane restoration-mode state. On the crashing path, plane 0 becomes `RESTORE_NONE` while at least one chroma plane remains enabled, so loop restoration stays on even though luma restoration is disabled."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_num_rows_lr_covers_active_chroma_rows",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "av1/common/thread_common.c",
      "function": "foreach_rest_unit_in_planes_mt",
      "line": 720,
      "operands": [
        "cm->rst_info[1].vert_units_per_tile",
        "num_rows_lr"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "cm->rst_info[1].vert_units_per_tile",
        "right": "num_rows_lr"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_root_sized_rows_cover_active_chroma_rows",
      "fine_trace_step": 7,
      "description": "The vulnerable sizing loop still iterates every plane after `av1_loop_restoration_filter_frame_init()` skipped disabled ones, reads `ctxt[plane].tile_rect`, and hardcodes the sequence superblock size instead of each active plane's parsed `restoration_unit_size`. That can make `num_rows_lr` smaller than the actual active-plane row count later used by `enqueue_lr_jobs()`, under-sizing both `cur_sb_col` and `job_queue`. The patch fixes both obligations here."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_enqueue_store_crosses_job_queue_capacity",
